-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/89873e07-6404-51cf-955e-cbac086bb013
-- title:
--   Connecting homomorphism from the Selmer group to the S-class group
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $R$ is a Dedekind domain with fraction field $K$, $S$ a set of height-one primes of $R$ and $n$ a natural number (positive where required). The $S$-class group is built as follows: `primeClass v` is the class of the ideal $v$ in `ClassGroup R`, `sClasses S` is the subgroup of `ClassGroup R` generated by $\{[v] : v \in S\}$, and `ClassGroupModS S` is the quotient $\mathrm{Cl}(R)/\langle [v] : v\in S\rangle$. Two normalisation lemmas record the translation between Mathlib's two ways of measuring a prime at a unit of $K$: $\mathrm{toAdd}\,(v.\mathrm{valuationOfNeZero}\,x)$ equals $-\,\mathrm{count}_v$ of the principal fractional ideal $xR$, whence $n$ divides one exactly when it divides the other.
--
--   The predicate `IsSel K S n x`, for $x \in K^\times$, says that $n \mid \mathrm{count}_v(xR)$ for every $v \notin S$; `isSel_of_mk_mem` and `mk_mem_of_isSel` identify this with membership of the class of $x$ in Mathlib's `selmerGroup` (abbreviated `Sel K S n` inside $Q_n = K^\times/(K^\times)^n$). The "$n$-th root ideal" is defined by exponents `radExp K S n x v`, equal to $0$ for $v\in S$ and to the integer quotient $\mathrm{count}_v(xR)/n$ otherwise; `rad` is the corresponding multipliable product $\prod_v v^{\mathrm{radExp}}$, a nonzero fractional ideal, `radU` its associated unit, and `radClass` its class in `ClassGroupModS S`. Under the hypothesis `IsSel` the exponents, hence `rad` and `radClass`, are multiplicative, `radClass` kills $n$-th powers, and `radClass` depends only on the class of $x$ modulo $(K^\times)^n$. The named datum is `connectingHom K S n : Sel K S n →* ClassGroupModS S`, sending an element of the Selmer group to `radClass` of a chosen representative in $K^\times$ (`rep`, via a quotient section); `connectingHom_apply_mk` evaluates it on the class of any $x$ satisfying `IsSel`. Auxiliary lemmas supply the factorisation of a unit fractional ideal as a finite product of the `primeUnit K v`, the vanishing of the class of a principal fractional ideal, and the criterion that a unit fractional ideal supported in $S$ has class in `sClasses S`.
--
--   **Relation to Mathlib.** Mathlib provides `IsDedekindDomain.selmerGroup`, `HeightOneSpectrum.valuationOfNeZeroMod` and `FractionalIdeal.count` but no comparison between `count` and `valuationOfNeZero`, and no map from the Selmer group to a class group; the $S$-class group `ClassGroupModS` and the homomorphism `connectingHom` are introduced here.
--
--   **Where it is used.** These definitions provide the ideal-theoretic side of the descent sequence $1 \to R_S^\times/(R_S^\times)^n \to K(S,n) \to \mathrm{Cl}_S(R)[n] \to 0$, with `connectingHom` the middle map; statements about its range, kernel and naturality are proved elsewhere in the development.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Definitions/Def_IsDedekindDomain_SelmerConnectingHom.lean

